## Suggested crate layout

```
/core       - Packet, Session, ResultEntry, FingerprintMethod trait, TriggerEvent enum
/capture    - PacketSource trait + pcap-file, live-interface, honeypot-log implementations
/dispatch   - session correlator, trigger classifier, worker pool dispatch engine
/methods    - one module per method (p0f adapter, ja3, ja4, ja4h, hassh, fusion, ...),
              each with its YAML manifest alongside it
/output     - batch mode + inference mode consumers, dashboard/CLI rendering
/cli        - binary entrypoint, argument parsing (source selection, mode flag, etc.)
```

Key crates to use: `serde` + `serde_yaml` (manifests), `pcap` or `etherparse`
(packet parsing), `tokio` (async dispatch + subprocess handling with timeouts),
`clap` (CLI).

